<title>GERMANY: VW halts Polo production in Spain.</title>
<headline>VW halts Polo production in Spain.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG said on Monday that it has halted production at its plant in Pamplona, Spain, because of delivery delays caused by the ongoing strike by Spanish truckers.</p>
<p>The plant produces about 1,000 Polo model cars daily, a spokesman for the company told Reuters.</p>
<p>VW said earlier on Monday that it would interrupt Polo production at its Wolfsburg plant as of Tuesday. Production of VW's popular Golf models would continue for the time being.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
